## Goal
- Provide a complete MCP store experience using the MCP Registry API, with health-checked servers, auth validation at merge time, and a clean UI that surfaces connection errors to the user.

## Constraints & Preferences
- Store server listing must use `https://registry.modelcontextprotocol.io/v0.1/servers` (with `version=latest` + cursor pagination)
- Package resolution must find the correct runtime command (`npx` for npm scoped packages, `uvx` for pypi)
- Remote-only servers (no npm/pypi package) must not be blocked; instead pre-fill Config JSON with `{"url": "...", "type": "streamable-http"}`
- When the Config JSON has `url` (instead of `command`), `confirmMerge` must send `remote_url` + `remote_transport` + `remote_headers` instead of `stdio_config`
- Auth headers from the registry (`remotes[].headers`) must be extracted as `environmentVariablesJsonSchema` and shown as env fields in the UI
- For remote servers *without* declared headers, show a single optional `Authorization` field (not the full custom-headers table)
- `StreamableHttpTransport` from `fastmcp.client.transports` is used to pass headers when connecting to remote servers; SSE bridges (stdio) must not use `StreamableHttpTransport`
- The namespace is auto-generated from the server name; no manual namespace input in the merge modal
- Quick-select presets (Excel, File System, SQLite, PDF) are commented out; only "Instalar a partir da loja" remains
- On dashboard load, each active server must be health-checked by fetching its spec URL(s); if unreachable, show "API indisponível"

